Changelog: 11-10-2026 09:24:18

BC250 Suite Releases becomes an app of its own, moved from tools/: the window (tools/release_ui.py, now bc250_suite_releases/main_window.py), the release logic (tools/release_plan.py, now plan.py), the board checks (tools/check-release.sh, now check-release.sh), its icon and its tests. It keeps the name, the app id bc250-release and its settings. run.sh starts it with the checkout's dev venv (--list prints the overview with the system python3); install.sh makes the launcher, menu entry and Desktop icon for this checkout. It has a .standalone marker (not in the portal) and a .checkout-only marker: it edits the checkout it lives in, so it has no releases, the release tool leaves it out and build_release.py refuses its tags. The footer shows its version and the checkout it edits.
